Inet sockets allow clients and servers to communicate across a network.  Unix sockets can be used to allow clients and servers on the same machine to communicate.  Though clients and servers on the same machine could communicate over an inet socket using localhost, unix sockets are much faster and use fewer system resources.  See the [unixsocketserver.html unixsocketserver] and [unixsocketclient.html unixsocketclient] examples.

